<html>
    <head>
        <title><TMPL_VAR NAME='home'></title>
        <style type="text/css" media="all">@import "/toss_designs/design.css";</style>
    </head>
    <body >
        <a name='form'></a>
        <h1>TOSS (<b>T</b>argeted <b>O</b>ligonucleotide <b>S</b>ilencer of <b>S</b>plicing) design parameters</h1>
        <p>
        
        <div class="tabs">
            <ul class="tabs primary">
                <li class="active"><a href="/cgi-bin/designs/index.pl?page=design_param&id=<TMPL_VAR name='GENEID'>&design=toss" class="active">Toss</a></li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        </p>
        <TMPL_IF name='ERRMSG'>
            <font color='red'>Error: <TMPL_VAR name = 'ERRMSG'></font>
        </TMPL_IF>
        <form name = 'edit' method='post'>
            <input type='hidden' name='page' value = 'do_design_toss'>
            <input type='hidden' name='id' value = '<TMPL_VAR name="GENEID">'>
            <div id='spec'>
                
                <fieldset>
                    <legend><b>A</b>lternatively <b>I</b>ncluded <b>R</b>egion (<b>AIR</b>) information</b></legend>
                    
                    <p>
                    Note: If you need help in identifying proper AIR sequence region, see information below submission form.
                    </p>
                    <div id='globalDiv'>
                        <div id='bspDiv'>
                        <table id='exon_bsp_tbl' border='0' cellpadding='5'>
                            <tr>
                                <td valign='top'>
                                    <span class="form-required" title="This field is required.">*</span>
                                    AIR:
                                </td>
                                <td>
                                    <textarea name='seq' rows='2' cols='100'></textarea>
                                    <div class="description">
                                    Paste the exact sequence of the AIR. Here is an example sequence for the SYK target gene:<br />
                                    ACTTGGTCAGCGGGTGGAATAATCTCAAGAATCAAATCATACTCCTTCCCAAAGCCTGGCCACAGAAAG
                                    </div>
                                </td>
                            </tr>
                        </table>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </fieldset>
            </div>
            <div class="description">Please note that a typical run takes around 30 seconds to complete.</div>
            <br/>
               
                <input type='submit' name='Launch' />
                <input type='reset' name='Reset' />
            </div>
        </form>
        <br/><br/>
        <p>
        The <b>UCS</b> is defined as the upstream constitutive sequence, the 
        <b>AIR</b> as the alternatively included region and 
        the <b>DCS</b> is defined as the downstream constitutive region. To
        identify the AIR sequence, you extract the sequence specific to the long splice 
        form. In the figure shows the AIR region is identified in gray for different 
        types of alternative splicing event.
        <br/><br/>
        <img src='/toss_designs/help.png' />
        <br/>
        Go <a href='#form'>back</a> to top of page.
        </p>
    </body>
</html>
